  "body": "Fixes #5444 — queue task 12827.\n\n**Problem:** the claim path could hand a worker a payload-less or schema-invalid packet (2026-11-04: a payload-null claim crashed a worker's claim loop), and `fleet queue list` had no `--lane`/`--worker` filters, so a crashed worker's live claims could not be enumerated before lease expiry.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Turso `verb_claim` (the live backend): the candidate SELECT now excludes payload-less rows (`payload IS NOT NULL AND payload <> '' AND payload <> '{}'`); a quarantine sweep at claim start moves pre-existing payload-less queued/parked rows in the queue to `blocked` with the reason in `last_error` and a `blocked` event row; every picked row must pass `validate_packet` — the same validator `/enqueue` runs (the oracle) — or it is quarantined and the pick moves to the next candidate / no-claim.\n- Client `claim_output`: defense in depth — a row carrying a `payload` field that is null or an empty object degrades to the distinguishable no-claim marker with a loud stderr line. Rows without a payload field keep the #5486 verbatim contract (existing tests unchanged).\n- `fleet queue list --lane/--worker`: filters applied end-to-end — client flags → broker request → Turso `verb_list` (`lane_id`/`worker_id`) and the PostgREST broker path (`lane_id=eq.`/`worker_id=eq.`).\n- `pm-stack/opencode-claimant/migration-0025.sql`: Postgres parity record for `claim_repo_task` (quarantine sweep + candidate payload predicate); schema validation stays in the broker/client layers that serve both stores.\n\n**Tests:** `cargo test -p fleet-queue --all-features --all-targets` — 99 + 2 passed on the laptop, including new invariant tests whose oracle is `validate_packet`: claim guard accepts a valid packet, rejects the three payload-less shapes (missing field / null / `{}`), and rejects schema-invalid packets. Live `--lane/--worker` verification follows once the broker binary carrying this build is deployed from main.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796731592&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7673&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7673&signature=1027ca51308cb710843dff2dc5a6be8a3258c3ee7d67d3d17a262baefe5318d3\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7673?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
